e'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T16:13:27-07:00","id":274237,"title":"","content":"Changeling, first edition anyway, has a huge list of recommended resources in the book. Of course it's twenty years out of date by now, but still...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:38:08-07:00","id":274714,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">For a more Broadway take on the Tzimisce, check out <i>Repo! The Genetic Opera</i>. <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Blood Points come in a little glass vial.<br /> A little glass vial? </span></i></span> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T18:25:16-07:00","id":275086,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think about The Prophecy for Demon the Fallen? any recomendations when it comes to books and short stories for DtF?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T18:29:58-07:00","id":275090,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I always thought the anime <i>Black Butler</i> has a good DtF vibe...</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T15:31:14-07:00","id":277601,"title":"","content":"The screwtape letters for playing a nephandi, or getting into how they think and temp mages (ditto for NWOD inferno-type demons).<br /> Dark City for Mage...really any mage.<br /> It's a pretty cheesy movie, but 'Ghost' for Wraith. The crazy guy on the train scene is a classic archetype of the tortured wraith.<br /> Pan's Labyrinth, of course, for Changling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T06:12:50-07:00","id":278772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273176-recomend-stuff-for-the-wod-movies-games-etc?p=275086#post275086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think about The Prophecy for Demon the Fallen? any recomendations when it comes to books and short stories for DtF?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The prophecy Serie as well as Gabriel and Legion would be good reference material...especially Gabriel. All of which was part of the movies recommanded in Demon The Fallen Corebook IIRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T01:31:42-08:00","id":362228,"title":"","content":"I ould recommend <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Sandman_%28Vertigo%29\" target=\"_blank\">The Sandman</a> series by Niel Gaiman for Changeling inspiration. There's also the Spiderwick Chronicles. It's nicely dark and tragic enough to get lots of good stories. <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucifer_%28DC_Comics%29\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer</a> is another good comic book series, Spin off that would have great material for Demon. For ambient music, I like to use Soundtracks by <a href=\"http://www.allmusic.com/artist/graeme-revell-mn0000198187\" target=\"_blank\">Greame Revell</a> and <a href=\"http://youtu.be/FtngZIBNBbE\" target=\"_blank\">Peter Gabriel.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T18:13:50-08:00","id":363084,"title":"","content":"Frailty and Boondock Saints, both for any Hunter game (Hunters Hunter or Reckoning), but also for the WoD in general.<br /> <br /> Supernatural tv show, mostly for inspiration and odd twists to old myths in the modern world. There is plenty sprinkled through for each line, though Seasons 4 or 5 onwards kind of loose the same feel.<br /> <br /> Silent Hill game, especially 1-3 makes for a pretty amazing short arch that can really ramp up the personal horror aspects, while the movies could give fodder for cults and conspiracies.<br /> <br /> The Matrix is basically a straight rip off of Mage through a different lens. Still, some room for ideas.<br /> <br /> The Maxx, both for Mage and Changling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T20:42:59-08:00","id":363177,"title":"","content":"i been thinking, Hotline Miami for a Vigilante Eucthanathos.<br /> Blair Witch Proyect for Nephandi<br /> Killer 7 and 100 Bullets for Euthanathos<br /> Fables for Changeling (?)<br /> Eagle Eye for Tecnocratic Union (?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-07-2015, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T07:41:14-08:00","id":363482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273176-recomend-stuff-for-the-wod-movies-games-etc?p=363177#post363177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been thinking, <b>Hotline Miami for a Vigilante Eucthanathos.</b><br /> Blair Witch Proyect for Nephandi<br /> Killer 7 and 100 Bullets for Euthanathos<br /> Fables for Changeling (?)<br /> Eagle Eye for Tecnocratic Union (?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hotline Miami is most certainly Slasher. It...it has to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T10:04:54-08:00","id":363629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273176-recomend-stuff-for-the-wod-movies-games-etc?p=363482#post363482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hotline Miami is most certainly Slasher. It...it has to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, Jacket was sent to kill Bad Guys, never civilians. people that the &quot;Phoners&quot; thought they were a threat<br /> <br /> I need confirmation from someone who runs Changeling.<br /> I have very briefly looked at the book, i havent gone any deeper but since its more &quot;Bright&quot; and with more Hope than the rest of the World of darkness, i been discussing with some friends and i have come up with this insane theory (bear up with me), That ...Digimon (Seasons 1 and 2) its the best example of the feeling of Changeling when it comes to kid characters, the sense of wander, dread, companions (the digimons being Chymeras). When they return to japan, the world was fill with mist and banity (mainly because of digimon dracula) but that sense and how they have to overcome all that...<br /> <br /> What you guys think about this insane rambling theory","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 01-08-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T03:36:17-08:00","id":364195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/273176-recomend-stuff-for-the-wod-movies-games-etc#post273176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">other than the ones on the books, what do you recomend as good influences for the WoD? . . . what authors, stories, movies, comics, videogames can you recomend for your favorite settings and worlds?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its no secret that Anne Rice's <b>Interview with the Vampire</b> had a big influence on <b>Vampire: the Masquerade</b>, but the game has influenced authors, too. I recently found Mario Acevedo's <b>X-Rated Bloodsuckers</b>, and the protagonist maps into the setting <i>beautifully. </i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>X-rated Bloodsuckers</b><br /> .<br /> When Felix Gomez returned from the War in Iraq with a disdain for daylight and a raging thirst for blood, he knew he couldn't settle for an ordinary 9-to-5 job. So after his discharge, the newly undead ex-infantryman chose the career that he felt best suited his vampiric tendencies: <i>private detective</i>.<br /> .<br /> Now he's been approached by sexy porn star Katz Meow, who wants Felix to investigate the murder of her once-equally agile friend and fellow toiler in the video sex-biz, Roxy Bronze. But his investigation into L.A.'s hardcore jungle is turning into a triple x-rated nightmare populated by hot babes, sleazy producers, sleazier politicians, sham evangelicals, and fanatical secret societies. And here on the seamy underside of Tinseltown, \u201cimmortal\u201d doesn't necessarily mean \u201cunkillable.\u201d </div> </div> </div>I even pulled out my copy of second edition, and Felix is a textbook Kindred (albeit with the &quot;Ingest Food&quot; merit), having Protean ****, Auspex **, and Dominate **. There's a bit of the first <i>Blade</i> movie mixed in (the whole sunblock thing), but otherwise, it would not surprise me at <i>all </i>to find out that Mr. Acevedo used <i>V:tM</i> to build his characters<br /> <br /> (Oh, and despite the provocative title and description, <i>X-Rated Bloodsuckers</i> is much less . . . &quot;adult&quot; than you'd expect. Its PG, maybe PG-13)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> . . . curious about changelling, any recomendations?</div> </div> </div> </div>For <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b>, take a look at Seanan McGuire's <i>October Daye</i> series. Ten bucks say that October Daye (the protagonist) was Ms. McGuire's character in a <i>Changeling</i> game, just aged up about ten years or so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rosemary and Rue</b><br /> <br /> The world of Faerie never disappeared; it merely went into hiding, continuing to exist parallel to our own. Secrecy is the key to Faerie's survival\u2014but no secret can be kept forever, and when the fae and mortal worlds collide, changelings are born. Outsiders from birth, these half-human, half-fae children spend their lives fighting for the respect of their immortal relations. Or, in the case of October &quot;Toby&quot; Daye, rejecting it completely. After getting burned by both sides of her heritage, Toby has denied the fae world, retreating into a \u201cnormal\u201d life. Unfortunately for her, Faerie has other ideas...<br /> .<br /> The murder of Countess Evening Winterrose, one of the secret regents of the San Francisco Bay Area, pulls Toby back into the fae world. Unable to resist Evening\u2019s dying curse, Toby must resume her former position as knight errant to the Duke of Shadowed Hills and begin renewing old alliances that may prove her only hope of solving the mystery...before the curse catches up with her. </div> </div> </div>There are a few tweaks to the setting, but everything about the plot screams, &quot;Changeling&quot;. The naming conventions (for the different fiefs), the magic (Toby even performs bunks!), key events . . . October &quot;Toby&quot; Daye won her spurs by finding a suitable site for the Queen of Mists new freehold . . .<br /> <br /> In the first novel, we briefly see Toby as a wilder . . . until her last quest blows up in her face, and she spends the next ten years exploring new career options . . . as a fish. She finally breaks free, only to find the mortal half of her life in ruins . . .and that somewhere along the lines, she's become a grump. She disavows her changeling heritage, tries to rebuild, and toys with sinking permanently into banality and just . . .forgetting. At least until the night when she came home to find a chilling message (and vicious <i>geas</i>) on her answering machine. A final command from a friend to, &quot;Find my killer, or die trying&quot; . . .<br /> <br /> Again, there are some tweaks to the setting, but its very, very easy to see Toby as a knight of House Liam, sworn to a duke from House Eiluned. And the author's gotten a whole series out it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":".  typo 01-09-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T15:36:41-08:00","id":364826,"title":"","content":"I find that the Neverwhere miniseries applies equally to old Changeling and new Changeling.<br /> <br /> I didn't like a lot of the artistic direction in it, but it's still pretty good at &quot;yeah there's this amazing world right here in the city you live in that you've never seen, and it's also terrifying sometimes&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T17:14:36-08:00","id":364912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have very briefly looked at the book, i havent gone any deeper but since its more &quot;Bright&quot; and with more Hope than the rest of the World of darkness </div> </div> </div>I love Changeling. But to say it's more bright or has more hope than the rest of WoD is just a huge disservice and faulty one at that. It has brightness to it in that all the colors and emotions are deeper and stronger but that includes the dark being darker and sorrow deeper as well. Also Changeling is in the end perhaps the least hopefull of all the gamelines. In it magic is dying, not in the future but right now and you are slowly withering away with it and there is literally no way to escape it or stop it. You can always try to escape Banality and the death of Magic by fleeing into the Dreaming but this only invites Bedlam, insanity, or you can try to weather it out in the Autumn World, our world, and slowly wither away. There is nigh mythical balance to be found which is the only real way out of these fates but there is only a single NPC who has ever achieved it and there is very little information on how to achieve it at all and no mechanics if I remember correctly. So it is basically unachievable goal unless the ST specifically wants you to be able to reach it. Golgonda, Ascension, Transcendence all of these have rules on how they are to be achieved and clear paths towards them not so for Changelings.<br /> <br /> Also back to the subject of light and dark. Changelings can be absolute monsters just as easily as they can be the knights in shining armour. One of my more memorable NPC's is Marrow a Bogie who feeds on human bone-marrow. He is nightmare incarnate able to walk past any electric security, use Cantrips to remain hidden from your sight and then murder you in your sleep only to carve the bones out of your body to feed on the lovely marrow inside and he is happy to do it while the rest of your family watches there bound onto their chairs. And that is what he does to get a good dinner you can guess how he is when someone get's to his bad side.<br /> <br /> Read up on some old fairy-tales in their original forms, no Disney versions or those censored for the modern child, and you'll get the idea of what the Dreaming is about. It's about grand heroics and horrible monsters, it is humanity's best and worst sides, it is both Dreams and Nightmares and that is without even bringing the Fomorians into the mix. Gaiman does a lot of good modern Changeling material, Caroline, Neverwhere etc.<br /> <br /> Fomorians on the other hand are those things that feed on the primal fears that even Banality cannot banish from the human mind, so ingrained are these fears that they might survive even humanity's downfall. There are fears ingrained in all living things and those fears are what the Fomorians feed upon.<br /> <br /> So no, I personally do not see Digimon as anything related to Changeling then again YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T19:06:54-08:00","id":369290,"title":"","content":"When it comes to <b>Mage</b>, its very tempting to rip off the animated series, <b>Xiaolin Showdown</b> - particularly the first season. Its not hard to see the four protagonists as Akashic Brothers (well, three Brothers, and one Sister) competing with an &quot;evil&quot; Orphan technomancer for control of a series of Artifacts known as the &quot;Shen Gong Wu&quot;. Second season, which introduces an Akashic <i>barabbi</i>, isn't bad, either. <br /> <br /> And while the anime <b>Bleach</b> doesn't fit well into any particular line, some parts of it do. Ichigo's efforts to reach &quot;Bankai&quot; (or the scenes arguing with Zangetsu) make for interesting Seekings (from <i>Mage</i>), for example. Elsewhere, the big duel against Byakuya Kuchiki (in the Soul Society arc) involves a near-textbook Catharsis (<i>a la</i> <b>Wraith</b>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}